{"title":"Guidelines for Voluntary Professional Data Science Certification","markdown":{"yaml":{"title":"Guidelines for Voluntary Professional Data Science Certification","subtitle":"American Statistical Association"},"headingText":"About This Document","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n\nThese guidelines, approved by the ASA Board of Directors on **September 30, 2024** and updated **January 23, 2026** and **March 5, 2026**, provide the framework for voluntary professional data science certification through the American Statistical Association.\n\n\nThe ASA offers two levels of voluntary data science certification:\n\n| Credential | Full Name | Experience Required |\n|---|---|---|\n| **DSP** | Data Science Professional | 2 years |\n| **AdvDSP** | Advanced Data Science Professional | 5 years |\n\nBoth credentials are **portfolio-based** (not examination-based), awarded through peer review of education, experience, and demonstrated competence aligned with the standards of the [Alliance for Data Science Professionals](https://alliancefordatascienceprofessionals.com/).\n\n::: {.callout-note}\n## Alliance for Data Science Professionals\n\nDSP and AdvDSP status is awarded based on criteria established by the **Alliance of Data Science Professionals**, a UK-based organization of which ASA is a member. If any contradiction exists between the requirements listed in this document and those of the Alliance, the Alliance's requirements prevail.\n:::\n\n## Quick Navigation\n\nThe guidelines cover:\n\n- **Eligibility**: [Level distinctions](chapters/02-level-distinctions.qmd), [Membership requirements](chapters/03-membership.qmd), [Education](chapters/05-educational-requirements.qmd), and [Experience](chapters/06-experience.qmd)\n- **Standards**: [Professional competence and skill areas](chapters/07-professional-competence.qmd)\n- **Process**: [Application form](chapters/09-application-form.qmd), [The DSCC](chapters/10-dscc.qmd), and [Appeals](chapters/11-appeals.qmd)\n- **Maintaining certification**: [Maintenance](chapters/12-maintenance.qmd), [Renewal](chapters/13-renewal.qmd)\n- **Governance**: [Disciplinary matters](chapters/15-disciplinary.qmd), [Conflict of interest](chapters/16-conflict-of-interest.qmd), [Public information](chapters/17-public-information.qmd)\n- **Appendix**: [Extended Skill Area Standards (A–E)](chapters/appendix-1.qmd)\n\n---\n\n**Additional details for applicants are found on the <a href=\"https://american-statistical-association.github.io/DSPCert/overview/\" target=\"_blank\">ASA data science certification website</a>.**\n","srcMarkdownNoYaml":"\n\nThese guidelines, approved by the ASA Board of Directors on **September 30, 2024** and updated **January 23, 2026** and **March 5, 2026**, provide the framework for voluntary professional data science certification through the American Statistical Association.\n\n## About This Document\n\nThe ASA offers two levels of voluntary data science certification:\n\n| Credential | Full Name | Experience Required |\n|---|---|---|\n| **DSP** | Data Science Professional | 2 years |\n| **AdvDSP** | Advanced Data Science Professional | 5 years |\n\nBoth credentials are **portfolio-based** (not examination-based), awarded through peer review of education, experience, and demonstrated competence aligned with the standards of the [Alliance for Data Science Professionals](https://alliancefordatascienceprofessionals.com/).\n\n::: {.callout-note}\n## Alliance for Data Science Professionals\n\nDSP and AdvDSP status is awarded based on criteria established by the **Alliance of Data Science Professionals**, a UK-based organization of which ASA is a member. If any contradiction exists between the requirements listed in this document and those of the Alliance, the Alliance's requirements prevail.\n:::\n\n## Quick Navigation\n\nThe guidelines cover:\n\n- **Eligibility**: [Level distinctions](chapters/02-level-distinctions.qmd), [Membership requirements](chapters/03-membership.qmd), [Education](chapters/05-educational-requirements.qmd), and [Experience](chapters/06-experience.qmd)\n- **Standards**: [Professional competence and skill areas](chapters/07-professional-competence.qmd)\n- **Process**: [Application form](chapters/09-application-form.qmd), [The DSCC](chapters/10-dscc.qmd), and [Appeals](chapters/11-appeals.qmd)\n- **Maintaining certification**: [Maintenance](chapters/12-maintenance.qmd), [Renewal](chapters/13-renewal.qmd)\n- **Governance**: [Disciplinary matters](chapters/15-disciplinary.qmd), [Conflict of interest](chapters/16-conflict-of-interest.qmd), [Public information](chapters/17-public-information.qmd)\n- **Appendix**: [Extended Skill Area Standards (A–E)](chapters/appendix-1.qmd)\n\n---\n\n**Additional details for applicants are found on the <a href=\"https://american-statistical-association.github.io/DSPCert/overview/\" target=\"_blank\">ASA data science certification website</a>.**\n"},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":false,"echo":true,"output":true,"warning":true,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"engine":"markdown"},"render":{"keep-tex":false,"keep-typ":false,"keep-source":false,"keep-hidden":false,"prefer-html":false,"output-divs":true,"output-ext":"html","fig-align":"default","fig-pos":null,"fig-env":null,"code-fold":"none","code-overflow":"scroll","code-link":false,"code-line-numbers":false,"code-tools":false,"tbl-colwidths":"auto","merge-includes":true,"inline-includes":false,"preserve-yaml":false,"latex-auto-mk":true,"latex-auto-install":true,"latex-clean":true,"latex-min-runs":1,"latex-max-runs":10,"latex-makeindex":"makeindex","latex-makeindex-opts":[